WEBVTT

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.150
This is my will.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.120
I've hidden the notebook in
the agreed-upon place.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.580
When needed, it will self-activate
and destroy the enemy.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.130
Understood.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.270
And have you mastered the
spirit-summoning spell?

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.760
I've rehearsed it again and again.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:27.060
Must I truly go?

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.770
It's... It hurts.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.010
Even though my life is in danger,

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:35.240
I don't want to lie to my
students and go into hiding.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:37.670
And the seventh month is almost upon us-

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:38.800
That's why.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.720
You have a higher task before you:

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.330
To find Nostradamus's Key and stop it.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:49.410
The enemy is, most likely, an evil force
that seeks to open the gate to Hell.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.520
But we don't know who it is yet.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.500
If attacks like last night's continue...

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.990
<b>I'll kill anyone in my way</b>

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.190
Then this is the only way.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.490
Must it be now?

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.830
I, myself, regret this, but...

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.680
I'm not ready for this yet.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.170
At least tell me where I'm going...

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:10.420
The magic will decide that.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.420
Please fulfill your duty!

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.250
<i>Longus quoquam!</i>

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:25.990
Where...

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:31.010
Where am I?

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.030
<b>Welcome to Sumida District</b>

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.030
<b>Sumida Tourism Center</b>

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.450
July 19th

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.460
<b>Notice:</b>

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.460
<b>School closed the 19th-20th, due to witchery.
The closing ceremony, on the 21st, proceeds as planned.
-The Principal</b>

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:51.460
My papa's...

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:53.020
Yes. He's alive.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.930
I don't know where he is,

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.980
but the Vice-Principal sent
him away with magic.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:00.050
My papa's alive...

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:07.560
Then he's still looking for
Nostradamus's Key.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.840
And he'll come back here in August.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.730
I can imagine the confused look on his face.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.400
I'll be able to see him.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:23.620
What will you do?

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:25.450
Are you going?

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.940
Y-Yeah. The mission's over...

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:33.790
And my peaceful future awaits
the return of its hero.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.420
What's wrong?

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.720
Nothing. I was just thinking
we'd be better off here

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.880
without you screwing up all the time.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.810
I should transfer... No, resign.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.990
I'll give a speech at the closing ceremony.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:49.100
See you there.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.630
Hello?

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.780
Oh, Uchida Fumiaki-kun's mother?

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.660
I'm sorry.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:05.740
Since we last spoke, we've been
too busy to call you...

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.130
Don't worry about it.

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:10.030
So regarding that appearance...

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:14.480
It will be at the closing ceremonies,
on the 21st, two days from now?

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.570
Spoon-bending?

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.960
Of course.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:24.920
I'd like to meet to discuss the particulars...

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.060
Yes, yes.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:38.700
Yes. Then I'll see you tomorrow at three.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.750
You invited my mom to the
closing ceremonies?

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.570
And Bunmei-kun, the spoon-bender.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.280
You wanted to see them, right?

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.790
I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.540
I wanted to surprise you.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.180
Wait a second...

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.830
I don't remember that.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:12.560
If I'd come here when I was
a kid, I should remember.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.210
It wouldn't be a surprise at all.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.860
But I've never been here before.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.550
Not even to Matsushiro.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.150
You saw my memories, right?

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.240
That's all I remember...

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:34.260
Come to think of it... Back then,
the footage suddenly blacked out.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.960
Bunmei! What's wrong?

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.170
Stop it...

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:41.410
Stop it!

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:44.250
Don't destroy my...

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.090
That's bad manners.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:53.130
That school seems kind of cool.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.060
Can I go with you tomorrow?

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.060
No.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.970
You have your summer homework.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:00.670
But...

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:03.070
Don't make me repeat myself.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:05.030
Here you are.

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:07.350
Oh. Hey, Bunmei-kun!

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.730
Are you Uchida Fumiaki-kun's mother?

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:11.410
Yes.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.060
I see him on TV all the time!

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.910
Um, can I have some chopsticks?

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.040
Chopsticks?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.400
Who eats curry with chopsticks?!

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:32.460
In other words, we ourselves
have destroyed the world?

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.020
That's impossible!

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.490
That's not what I'm saying.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.580
So what are you saying?

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.600
I'm investigating it right now!

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:41.530
History repeats, huh?

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:43.190
Probably true...

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:45.020
This is #6.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:46.300
There's something I want to ask you.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:47.230
Come in.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:49.200
What's going on, #6?

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.160
The closing ceremonies in two days...
The day of the prophecy...

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:55.290
Maya invited Uchida Fumiaki
here to perform.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:58.770
In other words, I'm going to see
myself when I was a kid.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.910
But I don't remember it at all.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.030
What is this?

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.810
So that's it?

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:08.760
Listen well, #6!

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.260
Do not, under any circumstances,
meet the younger you!

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.200
Don't meet the...

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.220
Why?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.560
There's a part of Information Science

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:18.170
called the Ramachandran-Fischer Conjecture.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.010
It states that there's a
limit to the amount of

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:23.260
information that can be processed
in a given space.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:27.120
When the amount of information passes a
certain threshold, it creates a rift in space-time.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.530
What are you talking about?

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:29.880
Explain it better.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:32.340
Take the "you" that came from the future

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.570
as a single set of information.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.730
The feedback of a massive
amount of information

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.480
from the future affects space-time itself.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:43.540
The information-processing creates
issues with the thermodynamics.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:47.420
With anyone else, it disappears
within normal fluctuations.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:51.470
But if you meet yourself,
the problems get far worse...

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.530
Creating a dimensional rift.

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:56.140
Does that mean...

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:56.810
Yes.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.850
You are Nostradamus's Key.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.200
To be precise, not you yourself,

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:06.800
but the act of you meeting
yourself in the past.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:11.320
It was probably the shock that made you
lose your memories from this time period.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.030
That's not funny.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:18.580
I found Nostradamus's Key and...

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:20.250
The future hasn't changed.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.710
We're still being invaded by aliens.

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:26.470
The future hasn't changed?

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:28.440
That's impossible!

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:29.510
Impossible.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:30.880
I...

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:32.970
<i>Bunmei!</i>

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.300
<i>She's Nostradamus's Key!</i>

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.700
You were in that picture, too, #6.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:40.380
That's why it worked.

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.330
But don't worry.

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:46.070
Now that we know the cause,
we just have to avoid it.

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:48.390
We'll transfer you back immediately.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:50.820
No, wait...

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.610
Let me stay here one more day!

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:55.420
My mom's coming tomorrow.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:57.580
I want to see her, at least.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.150
There'll still be a day left.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.450
Please!

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:05.390
What do we do, Commander Kumashiro?

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.840
That's why I never found it.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:24.170
There was no Key at the academy.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:26.880
<b>Disaster in Matsushiro, Nagano?!</b>

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.900
I knew this better than anyone.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.570
If there were,

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:33.240
it must've been brought after
I left the academy.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:40.160
That's why I sent in the
agent after my funeral.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.740
I never thought that this would, in itself,
be the start of everything.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:45.550
How ironic...

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.970
The future hasn't changed...

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:52.990
And meeting your child-self
is Nostradamus's Key...

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:54.970
I can't believe it.

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:57.100
Wait!

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:59.930
Then... Then I was the one who-

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:00.790
No!

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:01.810
It's not your fault!

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:06.080
It's not your fault at all.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:07.300
Bunmei...

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:12.280
I just have to not meet myself
when I was a kid.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.360
I got a day's reprieve.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:16.490
At least I can see my mom.

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.280
And it's thanks to you.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:19.570
Thank you.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.970
But I can't go to the closing ceremony.

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:26.780
Make up something to tell everyone.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.880
There's a way for you to go
to the closing ceremony.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.220
July 20th

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.180
Cancelled?

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:42.930
What is the meaning of this?

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.490
On the phone yesterday, you said
we were going ahead as planned!

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:47.070
Things have changed.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:48.390
Please leave.

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:49.520
Leave...

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:52.110
We came all the way from Tokyo!

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:54.150
All the way out here, to the
middle of nowhere...

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.700
How dare you treat us this way?!

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.900
What do you think my Fumiaki is?

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.620
I know all about your creepy little school.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.140
I bet you were just using him
to try and put on airs!

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:07.970
Who the hell do you think you are?!

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.290
Just a teacher here...

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:13.670
Forgive me,

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:17.130
but how do you think of your little Fumiaki?

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:20.910
Just as a goose that lays golden eggs, right?

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:24.250
I'll be speaking with a lawyer,

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:27.740
and you'll be seeing us in court!

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:33.730
Well?

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:37.310
If she's that mad, she'll
never come back here.

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:38.900
That was quite a performance.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.740
Now you'll be able to go to
the closing ceremonies.

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:44.360
No, not just the closing ceremonies...

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:47.200
If you wanted, you could stay here forever.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.250
No, I have to go back.

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.520
And I just realized,

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:57.670
I don't have any good memories
of my mom, but I love her.

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:00.340
If I stay here, I'll want to see her again.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.760
I'll want to go to Tokyo.

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:05.710
The risk of seeing myself when
I was a kid is too great.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:07.400
I'm sorry...

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.000
All right, then.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:12.900
There's one last thing I have to say to you.

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:15.030
These are the principal's orders!

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:17.500
We're going home, Fumiaki.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.530
What an awful school...

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:23.060
We should have never come
to a place like this.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:24.940
I'm sorry, Fumiaki.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:28.220
When we get back to Tokyo,
we can go see the planetarium...

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:29.500
Fumiaki?

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:37.470
Fumiaki!

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:53.710
Let's have a toast to Abe-sensei's future!

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:56.040
Cheers!

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:56.060
<b>Abe-sensei Farewell Party</b>

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.690
It's a shame, though...

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:04.720
Why are you quitting?

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:06.530
It was my suggestion.

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.420
He's not suited to being a teacher,

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:10.810
so why not take another path in life?

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.540
You're harsh. You know that?

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:16.730
So this is your last order to me?

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:17.700
What?

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:20.760
Just be thankful you're getting
a farewell party.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:24.060
But she's right. Teaching
is a lousy job for you.

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:24.720
That's true.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.470
You're not supposed to back her up there.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:30.270
I always liked you, though.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.770
Like that one time we fought those

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.440
little midget-demon things to save Ami.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:37.800
When was that?

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:40.150
When you were taking a nap
with all those skeletons.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:45.120
And when you jumped in front of my car

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.120
and shouted, "Take me to Maya-chan!"

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:49.470
When was that?

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:50.980
When you were being mind-controlled by

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:52.250
that witch and waving a torch around.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:55.930
You don't know enough about him, Dad.

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:58.670
Normally, he's just a wuss.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:01.250
Watch your mouth!

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:02.870
He does whatever anyone tells him.

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:06.800
And yet, he's got this cocky attitude,
and he's so irresponsible...

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.550
You shouldn't talk so big yourself.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:12.190
It wasn't so long ago that you were

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:13.850
wetting the bed and going, "Sorry, Daddy!"

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.110
How long ago was that?

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:17.010
And you, Maya-chan.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:19.550
I never knew anyone who loved
the occult as much as you,

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:21.720
but when I saw you again,
you claimed to hate it!

00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:24.720
I'm glad you're back to normal.

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:30.230
Anyway, the point is that people are
all different, and they all change.

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:31.450
Right, sensei?

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:32.290
Yeah.

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:35.190
There must've been a time

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:38.560
when you were a little hell-raiser, right?

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.880
No, I...

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:09.550
Vega! Altair! Deneb!

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:11.830
It's the summer triangle!

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.580
This is where I belong!

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:21.550
I guess I'm saying goodbye
to this place, huh?

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.420
Wuss, huh?

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:27.380
I really did just go along with things.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:28.800
Bunmei-kun!

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:30.200
Bunmei-kun!

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:41.900
I wonder if I ever did anything on my own.

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:55.290
It's my fault.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:58.250
It's all my fault.

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:00.430
By now, he must be...

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.140
July 21st

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:16.810
I'll be leaving for personal reasons.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:20.770
It was less than a month,

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:23.440
but I enjoyed the time I spent with you.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.110
Don't be foolish.

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:31.360
Don't just go along with what people say.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:35.930
And it's wrong to be cocky
and irresponsible.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:37.480
Hey, he just took that from me.

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:38.330
Yeah...

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:40.700
Keep your own two feet on the ground,

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:42.740
and follow your own path.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:45.100
That's all I have to say.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:08.030
That speech sucked.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:11.070
Of course it did.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:12.160
I wrote it.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:14.110
You took all that from Ami.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:15.410
Of course I did.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:18.030
I don't want them ending up like me.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:22.120
Do you hate yourself that much?

00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:26.460
I don't want to lie to myself anymore.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:34.880
I... What I love is...

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.230
Anyway, bye.

00:16:44.820 --> 00:16:46.530
This is #6.

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:47.030
Open the gate-

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:48.150
Wait! Don't go!

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:51.480
You're out of orders.

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:53.680
Don't go.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.100
Please don't go.

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:08.630
Maya...

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:11.000
No...

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:45.030
Did you come here alone?

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.090
By yourself?

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:50.840
I see.

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:53.130
That's fine then.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:56.140
Keep living like that.

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:16.740
Stop it!

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.330
Stop it!

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:25.470
Don't destroy my place!

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:28.390
Are you okay?

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:38.150
I'm taking this.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:53.820
Bunmei, we need to run.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:58.190
History changes, starting now!

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:00.910
Bunmei!

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:35.850
Maya!

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:37.020
Bunmei!

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:38.040
Maya...

00:19:38.310 --> 00:19:39.150
Take care...

00:19:40.710 --> 00:19:44.200
Take care of me!

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:46.870
Bunmei!

00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:13.000
Bunmei...

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.950
We found the Key and destroyed it.

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:30.710
Where am I?

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:32.980
Stand up.

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:34.960
With your own two feet.

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:00.360
Everyone, come outside!

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:11.060
Maya...

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:39.610
<b>Maya</b>

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:42.410
Maya?

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:43.320
Is that you?

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:44.640
What?

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:46.030
What's wrong, Papa?

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:47.330
Did something happen?

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:51.340
Where are you?

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:57.790
Um... I was getting some tea.

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:59.280
I'll head home.

00:21:59.610 --> 00:22:00.920
I'm glad.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:03.510
Fumiaki said he'd be home early today.

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:05.760
We can all have dinner together.

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:09.130
Yeah... Yeah, that'll be nice.

00:22:09.130 --> 00:22:11.000
I'll be home right away.

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:12.790
Right away.

00:23:56.780 --> 00:23:59.750
<b>Uchida</b>

00:23:56.950 --> 00:23:58.080
I'm home.

00:23:58.460 --> 00:23:59.750
Welcome back.

00:24:02.110 --> 00:24:03.530
Good timing.

00:24:04.180 --> 00:24:05.930
Let's all eat.

00:24:09.940 --> 00:24:14.930
The End

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:19.510
This program is a work of fiction.
Departed spirits, psychic abilities,
aliens, UMAs, etc., do not exist.

00:24:16.430 --> 00:24:21.510
Unless you believe in them...
